<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Najd</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Nejd</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Najd is the central plateau region of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabian-peninsula">Arabian Peninsula</a>, today the heart of Saudi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a>, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/riyadh">Riyadh</a> as its main city. A land of oases, wadis and desert, it was the birthplace of the 18th-century reform movement of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-ibn-abd-al-wahhab">Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahhab</a> and the home of the successive Saudi states. In the 19th century the Rashidis of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hail">Ha'il</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-saud">Al Saud</a> fought for control of it.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/najd.jpg" alt="Najd" width="320" height="196" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: saudipics · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tuwaiq.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
